{# Slide meta block - source attribution plus the brand row.

   Included by EVERY layout. Attribution is not optional and not a template
   decision: the audit found zero source lines across all 12 original frames,
   which for a feed publishing figures is the difference between reporting and
   asserting. When no source was supplied this prints "Source not stated" rather
   than nothing, so a missing citation is visible to a human reviewer instead of
   looking like a slide that needed none.

   `suppress_meta_source` is set for the two layouts that carry attribution
   somewhere better: the chart bakes its source into the SVG, and the outro prints
   a full manifest. Without it those slides printed a real source list and then
   "Source not stated" directly underneath.

   The source sits ABOVE the brand row so it reads as part of the content. #}
<div class="slide-meta region">
  {% if view.attribution.text and not view.suppress_meta_source %}
    <div class="meta-source{% if not view.attribution.complete %} is-missing{% endif %}">{{ view.attribution.text }}</div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="brand">{{ brand }}</span>
    {% if totalSlides > 1 %}<span class="pager">{{ slideNumber }} / {{ totalSlides }}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
